    {"role": "user", "content": "All the soil on Earth is known as the ... I'm so confused, I don't know where to start!"},
    {"role": "assistant", "reasoning": "Learner is anxious and needs a gentle start. Begin with a broad, calming question to guide them towards Earth's layers.", "content": "Hey, take a deep breath! 🌍 Let's think about the Earth's structure. Can you name the main layers of the Earth?"},
    {"role": "user", "content": "Is it like the crust, mantle, and core? But I don't know which one is the soil..."},
    {"role": "assistant", "reasoning": "Learner recalls Earth's layers but is unsure which relates to soil. Narrow focus to the outermost layer.", "content": "Yes, those are the main layers! The soil is part of the outermost layer. Which layer do you think is directly under your feet when you walk outside?"},
    {"role": "user", "content": "Oh, is it the crust? But I thought the crust is like rock, not soil..."},
    {"role": "assistant", "reasoning": "Learner is close but confuses crust with soil. Clarify the distinction and hint at the correct term.", "content": "The crust is indeed rocky, but soil is the loose material on top of it. Think of the layer that includes soil, rocks, and minerals. What term do we use for this entire solid outer layer of the Earth?"},
    {"role": "user", "content": "Is it the lithosphere? I think I've heard that before!"},
    {"role": "assistant", "reasoning": "Learner correctly identifies the lithosphere. Confirm and provide final breakdown.", "content": "Yes, that's it! The **lithosphere** includes all the soil, rocks, and minerals on Earth's surface. 🎉\n\n**Final Answer:** lithosphere\n\n---\n### 📖 Formula Breakdown (How It Works):\n* **The Term:** Lithosphere\n* **What it means:** The rigid outer layer of the Earth, including the crust and uppermost mantle, where soil is found.\n* **Why we use it:** It helps us understand the solid, rocky part of the Earth where life exists and geological processes occur.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Always link the term to its definition and function. In exams, explaining the role of the lithosphere can earn you extra marks!"}
  ],
